  63:     - The frame interior contains a dominant background color and one foreground object color.
  64:     - Some object boundaries contain five-pixel plus-shaped background notches.
  65: 
  66:     Rule
  67:     - Find every background plus whose opposite side is supported by foreground object pixels and whose open side faces one frame side.
  68:     - Recolor the five pixels of that plus with the color of the facing frame side.
  69:     - Leave all other pixels unchanged.
  70: 
  71:     Key insight
  72:     The frame side colors are direction labels for the open notches in the foreground object.
  73:     """
